flags: -O

--- OUT --->
3
--- IR --->
// the window's length and data pointer are loaded **once, in the entry block** - the cursor holds its
// bound by value, so nothing in the loop can have written them and LICM may hoist both. that is what
// gives the loop a computable trip count, and with it unrolling and vectorisation
CHECK: define i32 @_totalZZMRBMLC5arrayIMLPiE
CHECK: entry:
CHECK: load i64
CHECK: load ptr

// and the body holds no calls at all: `iterate`, `advance` and `current` are inlined away, the cursor
// struct is SROA'd to a single register, and the bounds assert is gone with the release build. what is
// left is the indexed load and the loop's own compare - the same loop a hand-written cursor produces
CHECK: body:
CHECK-NOT: call
CHECK: getelementptr i32
CHECK-NOT: call
CHECK: br i1
